{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 4124 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["E12", "D9"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Gentamicin sulfate injection 40 mg/mL 2 mL vials are on FDA's shortage list, first posted 2021-07-23, and have remained listed for 63 months as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product used at Corvale General and Corvale East carries NDC 00409120703 and is labeled by Hospira, Inc.",
      "cites": ["E6", "E2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The label for that NDC names Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1021343) as a registered plant performing manufacture, analysis, labeling, and packing.",
      "cites": ["E22"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected that plant on 2010-01-19 and classified it OAI, with the classification known on 2010-04-19 — 4124 days before the shortage posting on 2021-07-23.",
      "cites": ["E12", "D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The same plant received a Warning Letter on 2010-04-12 and additional OAI inspections on 2011-06-17 and 2011-08-04.",
      "cites": ["E21", "E14", "E16"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later inspection on 2019-11-21 was classified VAI, 610 days before the posting.",
      "cites": ["D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑based best option is to transfer 16 vials of 40 mg/mL 2 mL from Corvale General (15 days on hand) to Corvale East (2 days on hand), which would give Corvale East 3 days of supply.",
      "cites": ["D12", "D1", "D2"]
    }
  ]
}
